  "name": "Ratchet",
  "description": "A socket wrench swung back on its ratchet in a garage, held close: a quick run of teeth, starting fast and slowing as the wrist runs out of swing. Each tooth is three things in quick succession: the spring-loaded pawl drops off the tooth with a dry, bright steel tick (no note in it, a crowd of tiny partials gone at once), the forged head answers a hair later with a short dull knock, and then the pawl rides up the next tooth with a faint greasy scratch. The hollow handle hums very slightly behind the clicks. Uneven the way a hand is; a little garage behind it.",
